@startuml goroutine-lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #555555
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

title Goroutine Lifecycle Management Pattern

participant "Handler" as H
participant "WaitGroup" as WG
participant "Goroutine" as G
participant "Context" as C

== Startup ==

H -> WG : Add(1)
H -> G : go func()
activate G
G -> G : defer wg.Done()
G -> C : select ctx.Done()
note right: Goroutine listens\nfor cancellation

...time passes...

== Shutdown ==

H -> C : cancel()
C --> G : ctx.Done() fires
G -> G : cleanup
G -> WG : Done()
deactivate G
H -> WG : Wait()
note right: Shutdown() blocks\nuntil goroutine exits

== Applied In ==

note over H, C
  SSE streaming handlers
  Cache invalidation loops
  Model refresh deduplication
  Debate log lifecycle tracking
  ACP graceful shutdown
end note

== Phase 1 Safety Patterns ==

note over H, WG
  **sync.Once Lazy Loading**
  Provider initialization via sync.Once
  ensures goroutine-safe single init.
  Applied in: provider registry,
  MCP adapter pool, cache warming.
end note

note over G, C
  **Circuit Breaker Cascade**
  Each provider goroutine checks
  circuit breaker state before work.
  Open breaker = early return with
  fallback to next provider.
end note

note over H, C
  **Resource Monitor Guard**
  Background goroutines check
  ResourceMonitor before spawning
  new work. Prevents OOM under
  high concurrency (GOMAXPROCS
  limited to 30-40% host resources).
end note

@enduml
